.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt RAVEN-CONFIG 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm raven-config
.Nd validate and show the RavenBSD TOML configuration
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm check
.Nm
.Cm show
.Nm
.Cm get Ar dotted.key
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the fixed configuration directories of
.Pa architecture/17-modern-userland.md
section 4.1:
compiled defaults, the selected profile, the main
.Pa /etc/raven/raven.toml
and the sorted
.Pa /etc/raven/conf.d/*.toml
drop-ins.
Tables merge recursively; scalars and arrays replace and a
.Dv null
overlay removes a key.
Unknown keys, wrong types and paths that are not absolute or contain
.Pa ..
are errors with the file and key; the loader never expands the environment or evals shell text.
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width "get dotted.key"
.It Cm check
Parse every file and report the result; a parse or schema failure exits 1.
This check is also part of
.Nm raven doctor
and the image-build gate.
.It Cm show
Print the effective configuration as TOML, or as the
.Va kind :
.Dq config
JSON object with
.Fl -json .
.It Cm get Ar dotted.key
Print one effective value.
.El
.Pp
Size values are integer bytes or strings such as
.Dq "8 MiB" ;
durations are integer milliseconds or strings such as
.Dq "250ms" .
A configured secret file must not be world-readable.
The configuration format is documented once in
.Pa architecture/17-modern-userland.md ;
this page is the command summary.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A configuration or missing-key error exits 1; a usage error exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr raven 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD modern userland contract, revision 1.
